    "summary": "Tight Bird Song → Let It Grow > Deal flow, strong Garcia and Brent",
    "blurb": "The show shines with a soaring Bird Song into the Let It Grow → Deal sequence and a punchy Iko Iko → Miracle → Stella Blue → Good Lovin’ run. Jerry’s guitar is crisp and inspired while Brent’s keyboards sparkle throughout, keeping the band tight and energetic.",
    "review": "May 13, 1981 at Providence Civic Center delivered a quintessential early‑'80s Dead experience. The first set built momentum with Jack Straw kicking things off before the band launched into an electrifying Bird Song that seamlessly segued into Let It Grow and a soaring Deal—highlighted by Jerry’s blistering solo and Brent’s shimmering keys. The second set kept the energy high, moving from the majestic Terrapin Station through a compact yet potent Iko Iko → Miracle transition into Stella Blue and a rousing Good Lovin’ finale, before closing sweetly with Brokedown Palace. Across multiple recordings the performance is praised for its tightness, strong vocal harmonies, and especially the standout keyboard work; even the post‑drum section receives nods for its punchy drive. While a few reviewers note a slightly shorter second half compared to other ’81 shows, the overall flow remains compelling, making this concert a solid entry in the era’s catalog.\n\nFor listeners seeking the clearest representation, the Miller soundboard (gd1981-05-13.sbd.miller.86780.sbeok.flac16) offers excellent balance and detail, capturing the band’s tight interplay without any noticeable drop‑outs or muddiness.",
